Delete All Occurrences of a Key in Doubly Linked List

Optimal Solution

Approach:
Traverse the doubly linked list using a pointer temp.
For every node, check if its value is equal to the target value.
If the current node contains the target:
Store its previous node and next node.
If it is the head node, update the head.
Connect the previous node with the next node.
Update the prev pointer of the next node.
Delete the current node.
Move temp to the next node.
If the current node is not the target, simply move to the next node.

Idea: Whenever we find the target value, remove that node and reconnect its neighbours.

Time Complexity: O(n)
We traverse the linked list only once.

Space Complexity: O(1)
No extra space is used.

Code :

class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* deleteAllOccurrences(ListNode* head, int target) {

        ListNode* temp = head;

        while (temp != NULL) {

            if (temp->val == target) {

                // Store previous and next nodes
                ListNode* prevNode = temp->prev;
                ListNode* nextNode = temp->next;

                // If deleting the head node
                if (temp == head) {
                    head = nextNode;
                }

                // Connect previous node with next node
                if (prevNode != NULL) {
                    prevNode->next = nextNode;
                }

                // Update previous pointer of next node
                if (nextNode != NULL) {
                    nextNode->prev = prevNode;
                }

                // Delete current node
                delete temp;

                // Move to next node
                temp = nextNode;

            } 
            else {
                temp = temp->next;
            }
        }

        return head;
    }
};


